# =========================
# pkg AUTODIFF parameters :
# =========================
#  inAdExact :: get an exact adjoint (no approximation) (def=.True.)
#
 &AUTODIFF_PARM01
# inAdExact = .FALSE.,
# useKPPinAdMode: KPP is not compiled (see data.pkg), and pkg/autodiff ANDs this switch with useKPP
# (autodiff_readparms.F), so it has no effect. Set it again only with KPP restored: .FALSE. keeps KPP
# in the forward sweep and out of the adjoint sweep.
# useKPPinAdMode = .FALSE.,
# Live since 2026-09-11, when data.pkg turned GM/Redi on: GM acts in the forward sweep and in every
# recomputation of it, and not in the adjoint sweep, where its linearisation blows up within days
# (stability_study, 31236). It acts on what Tapenade records after FORWARD_STEP applies it: in every
# checkpoint-everything build, and in the nocheckpoint build since its list of 2026-09-12 keeps the routines
# that read it checkpointed (the submit body refuses a list build not recorded as safe).
 useGMRediInAdMode = .FALSE.,
# Since 2026-09-10: the adjoint sweep linearises about the unlimited DST3 (scheme 30) while the
# forward sweep keeps the flux-limited scheme 33 of data -- the flux limiter's adjoint is what
# blew up every long adjoint here (stability_study, runs 31166/31167/31176). Every adjoint build
# compiles the replacement: for the horizontal and explicit vertical fluxes in
# mods_tapenade_hooks/gad_advection.F (since 2026-09-12), and for implicit vertical advection in
# code_tap/gad_implicit_r.F (since 2026-09-12; before that only the approxAdv build carried it).
# The submit body refuses a DINO adjoint namelist without this switch, or without
# useGMRediInAdMode=.FALSE. while data.pkg turns GM/Redi on, unless IMPACTS_ALLOW_EXACT_ADJOINT=1
# (check_staged_namelists in scripts/setup_params.sh; since 2026-09-12).
 useApproxAdvectionInAdMode = .TRUE.,
 &
